When i posted my YAFAP 2 months ago Philip Lucas told me, that with
more preparations to final run i "should have a pretty easy Val/Bar
ascension coming up. Well, hopefully.". This proved to be true.
I played priests for several weeks, but they are hard to keep alive in
a mid game. One of those priest made it (with almost full ascension
kit) to the Gehennom, but met - first time in my live - Demogorgon and
learned hard way why he is so respected opponent.
So i tried Valkyrie instead. And this was easy.
Game began uneventfully, with Sokoban first and than Gnomish Mines.
Some hearse bone files gave me blessed luckstone. I had 4 or 5 aligned
altars in the first 10 levels, so i got Mjollnir and kept it until
Castle as a main weapon. I had some nice artifact weapons including
Stormbringer from Hearse bones in lower mines, but didn't use it until
later. Wishing from throne somewhere near DLV 25 gave me SDSM. I had
lots of stuff, and there was only one little problem - no scroll of
identify was generated. I kept stashing all that in Mines Town, but
only very late found something which could be price identified as
identify scroll. After that things got even easier, because in Moloch
Sanctum i found second (after castle) wand of wishing and magic
marker.
BTW i found boots of speed within 30 turns after i wished for them.
This was not a problem, since I used 10 wishes overall, and had at
least 7 more saved "for later" (wand and 2 magic lamps).  Most of my
wishes was magic markers and wands of death, which i used often and
wisely.
I decided not to bother with books - Valkyria was pathetic in
spellcasting anyway. I read two blessed books i found, because i
needed some nice way of getting confused , and trying to cast a
forgotten spell is a very good one.
I decided not to bother with gems either. I do not play for high
score, and they are useless for all the rest.
Because everything was going so smoothly i tried my first ever
voluntary challenges, and decided to try no polymorphing myself or
objects. This is not particularly challenging if you have so many
wishes to burn, but hey, you have to start somewhere.
I never felt in danger during this game. Even when i got to DLV 40
bone files of my priest with Yeenoghu, Demogorgon and Orcus right next
to stairs i simply returned back upstairs, got prepared, and dealt
with them in few turns.  This bones gave me redundant ascension kit
and incredible amount of artifacts, including Mitre of Holiness and
Staff of Aesculapius (which evaded my grasp). Look below what i had to
carry all the way astral plane!
I carried all stuff to my stash and prepared to final run properly.
Did nurse dancing, drank all potions of gain level, got crowned after
sacrificing fiesta. Genocided all L and ;. As a gnome couldn't
genocide all h, but wiped out the most annoying members of my family
tree.  I got rid with my pets too, but this wasn't planned.
Stormbringer killed them all, and when i realized what's going on, it
was too late. Stormbringer was a very effective weapon, especially
twoweaponing with silver saber, so i decided to keep it instead.
Final run was much easier than i thought. Mysterious force was
annoying, and malignant aura needed some reaction, but everything was
fine. I decided to Planes with conflict, which proved to be effective
strategy in my first ascension. Even Astral was not a challenge at
all. I just whacked Death to death when i met her, and did the same to
other two riders. The last altar was mine.
Here i made the only mistake in the whole game - i offered my god
cheap plastic imitation instead of real amulet. But survived
that.

